1
00:00:04,375 --> 00:00:06,435
Last time, we counted legs.

2
00:00:06,705 --> 00:00:08,085
Insects have six.

3
00:00:08,355 --> 00:00:11,465
And we met the reptiles, with dry, scaly skin.

4
00:00:11,745 --> 00:00:12,855
Like Basil!

5
00:00:12,908 --> 00:00:14,428
Cold-blooded, and proud!

6
00:00:18,758 --> 00:00:19,978
Lock in first.

7
00:00:20,258 --> 00:00:21,718
And find the new lizard!

8
00:00:25,033 --> 00:00:25,913
Round one.

9
00:00:26,213 --> 00:00:27,823
This animal has wings.

10
00:00:28,103 --> 00:00:29,103
It flies.

11
00:00:29,383 --> 00:00:30,593
Is a bat a bird?

12
00:00:30,913 --> 00:00:31,993
One, yes.

13
00:00:32,263 --> 00:00:33,123
Two, no.

14
00:00:33,413 --> 00:00:34,893
Show me with your fingers.

15
00:00:40,359 --> 00:00:41,339
Locked in!

16
00:00:41,467 --> 00:00:42,087
One!

17
00:00:42,227 --> 00:00:43,677
It flies, like a bird!

18
00:00:43,728 --> 00:00:44,488
Two!

19
00:00:44,578 --> 00:00:46,138
I think I see fur.

20
00:00:46,184 --> 00:00:46,974
Two.

21
00:00:47,244 --> 00:00:48,464
No feathers.

22
00:00:48,886 --> 00:00:49,766
Be a hair!

23
00:00:50,056 --> 00:00:51,036
Shrink down.

24
00:00:51,316 --> 00:00:52,246
Quietly.

25
00:00:54,537 --> 00:00:56,724
You are one hair on a fruit bat's back.

26
00:00:57,207 --> 00:00:59,991
Soft fur, like a forest, all around you.

27
00:01:00,556 --> 00:01:02,016
It spreads its wings.

28
00:01:02,466 --> 00:01:03,476
Thin skin.

29
00:01:03,916 --> 00:01:05,066
No feathers!

30
00:01:05,654 --> 00:01:06,484
Whoosh!

31
00:01:06,964 --> 00:01:08,244
Out into the night.

32
00:01:08,664 --> 00:01:09,894
The air is cool.

33
00:01:10,304 --> 00:01:12,314
But the body under you stays warm.

34
00:01:12,966 --> 00:01:16,536
Back at the palm, a baby bat drinks its mother's milk.

35
00:01:18,958 --> 00:01:20,268
The answer is two.

36
00:01:20,548 --> 00:01:22,028
A bat is not a bird.

37
00:01:22,318 --> 00:01:23,518
It is a mammal!

38
00:01:26,379 --> 00:01:27,409
Two fingers?

39
00:01:27,679 --> 00:01:28,899
One finger up!

40
00:01:28,947 --> 00:01:29,577
Fur!

41
00:01:29,747 --> 00:01:30,857
Not feathers!

42
00:01:31,279 --> 00:01:32,499
Say it with me!

43
00:01:33,212 --> 00:01:37,652
Mammals are animals that have hair or fur as their outer covering.

44
00:01:40,288 --> 00:01:42,388
Monkeys, cats, bats, and you!

45
00:01:42,658 --> 00:01:44,208
They all have hair or fur.

46
00:01:44,261 --> 00:01:45,801
Pip and I are mammals!

47
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:47,080
And I'm the reptile.

48
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,480
No fur for me!

49
00:01:48,826 --> 00:01:51,396
Most mammals give birth to their young alive.

50
00:01:51,676 --> 00:01:56,096
The females have mammary glands that can produce milk for their young.

51
00:01:59,312 --> 00:02:04,762
Mammals are warm-blooded, which means that they can maintain a constant body

52
00:02:04,512 --> 00:02:05,452
temperature.

53
00:02:09,576 --> 00:02:10,656
Exam tip!

54
00:02:10,946 --> 00:02:12,566
Compare a bat and a bird.

55
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:15,930
A bat and a bird are similar because both have wings.

56
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:19,350
They are different because a bat has fur, but a bird has

57
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:19,870
feathers.

58
00:02:21,389 --> 00:02:22,399
Round two.

59
00:02:22,679 --> 00:02:24,199
Which one does not belong?

60
00:02:24,499 --> 00:02:25,619
One, a cat.

61
00:02:25,899 --> 00:02:27,079
Two, a monkey.

62
00:02:27,349 --> 00:02:28,649
Three, a lizard.

63
00:02:28,939 --> 00:02:30,419
Show me with your fingers.

64
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:36,869
Locked in!

65
00:02:36,997 --> 00:02:37,887
Two.

66
00:02:38,017 --> 00:02:39,137
The monkey.

67
00:02:39,267 --> 00:02:40,717
It climbs trees.

68
00:02:40,766 --> 00:02:41,466
Three!

69
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:42,816
No fur.

70
00:02:42,869 --> 00:02:43,569
Three!

71
00:02:43,699 --> 00:02:44,719
Like me!

72
00:02:44,916 --> 00:02:46,276
The answer is three.

73
00:02:46,566 --> 00:02:48,056
Find what the others share.

74
00:02:48,346 --> 00:02:51,016
A cat and a monkey have fur: mammals.

75
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:54,526
A lizard has dry, scaly skin: a reptile.

76
00:02:54,576 --> 00:02:55,666
Three fingers?

77
00:02:55,936 --> 00:02:57,146
One finger up!

78
00:02:57,196 --> 00:02:57,836
Oops.

79
00:02:58,216 --> 00:02:59,656
Cats climb too!

80
00:02:59,665 --> 00:03:00,865
Scales, not fur.

81
00:03:01,005 --> 00:03:02,475
The odd one out is me!

82
00:03:03,974 --> 00:03:04,604
One.

83
00:03:04,354 --> 00:03:06,224
It has scaly skin.

84
00:03:06,364 --> 00:03:06,974
Two.

85
00:03:07,204 --> 00:03:09,034
It breathes air with its lungs.

86
00:03:09,084 --> 00:03:09,684
Three.

87
00:03:10,044 --> 00:03:12,334
It swims in the sea, so it is a fish!

88
00:03:12,611 --> 00:03:13,511
Showdown!

89
00:03:13,821 --> 00:03:14,951
Double points.

90
00:03:15,221 --> 00:03:16,841
One line has a mistake.

91
00:03:17,131 --> 00:03:18,891
Line one, two, or three?

92
00:03:19,191 --> 00:03:20,661
Show me with your fingers.

93
00:03:27,136 --> 00:03:28,116
Locked in!

94
00:03:28,244 --> 00:03:28,704
Three.

95
00:03:29,314 --> 00:03:31,504
Fish usually breathe through gills.

96
00:03:31,555 --> 00:03:32,325
Three!

97
00:03:32,355 --> 00:03:33,585
That's my group!

98
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:34,250
Oops!

99
00:03:35,121 --> 00:03:36,471
Read all the clues.

100
00:03:36,751 --> 00:03:39,311
Scaly skin and lungs: a reptile.

101
00:03:39,671 --> 00:03:40,961
It is a sea turtle!

102
00:03:41,092 --> 00:03:42,452
Showed three fingers?

103
00:03:42,732 --> 00:03:44,632
Put up two more on your score hand!

104
00:03:44,684 --> 00:03:45,364
Fixed!

105
00:03:45,970 --> 00:03:47,500
Six animal groups!

106
00:03:48,295 --> 00:03:49,396
Say it with us!

107
00:03:50,056 --> 00:03:50,966
Six legs?

108
00:03:50,936 --> 00:03:51,806
Insect!

109
00:03:53,656 --> 00:03:54,726
Dry, scaly skin?

110
00:03:54,536 --> 00:03:55,486
Reptile!

111
00:03:57,256 --> 00:03:58,166
Hair or fur?

112
00:03:58,136 --> 00:03:58,972
Mammal!

113
00:04:00,856 --> 00:04:01,766
Six legs?

114
00:04:01,736 --> 00:04:02,606
Insect!

115
00:04:02,656 --> 00:04:03,726
Dry, scaly skin?

116
00:04:03,536 --> 00:04:04,486
Reptile!

117
00:04:04,456 --> 00:04:05,366
Hair or fur?

118
00:04:05,336 --> 00:04:06,172
Mammal!

119
00:04:06,861 --> 00:04:08,011
Exam corner!

120
00:04:08,284 --> 00:04:09,584
Say it with me!

121
00:04:10,295 --> 00:04:15,425
Living things such as plants and animals can be classified based on

122
00:04:15,175 --> 00:04:17,615
common observable characteristics.

123
00:04:18,045 --> 00:04:20,485
There are different types of plants and animals.

124
00:04:23,123 --> 00:04:24,593
Show me your score hand!

125
00:04:24,873 --> 00:04:25,903
More than two?

126
00:04:26,183 --> 00:04:27,563
You beat the Buddies.

127
00:04:27,833 --> 00:04:28,943
Four fingers?

128
00:04:29,213 --> 00:04:30,223
High five!

129
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:32,368
Did you spot the little lizard?

130
00:04:32,648 --> 00:04:33,868
It was by the lamp.

131
00:04:34,188 --> 00:04:36,628
Is it cold-blooded, or warm-blooded?

132
00:04:36,888 --> 00:04:38,208
Tell someone at home.

133
00:04:39,092 --> 00:04:41,382
Next time: fungi and bacteria!

134
00:04:41,672 --> 00:04:42,882
Mould on bread.

135
00:04:43,182 --> 00:04:44,902
Yeast, for making bread.

136
00:04:45,172 --> 00:04:46,432
Both are fungi!

137
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:48,122
Which one is useful?

138
00:04:48,392 --> 00:04:49,712
Lock in your answer!

139
00:04:50,434 --> 00:04:52,634
Let's read today's key words together!

140
00:04:52,924 --> 00:04:53,684
Ready?

141
00:04:54,021 --> 00:04:54,748
Mammals.

142
00:04:56,234 --> 00:04:57,494
Mammary glands.

143
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:00,200
Warm-blooded.

144
00:05:01,742 --> 00:05:02,682
Well done!

145
00:05:03,664 --> 00:05:04,768
Say it with us!

146
00:05:05,569 --> 00:05:06,319
Ready?

147
00:05:06,442 --> 00:05:07,102
One!

148
00:05:07,442 --> 00:05:08,142
two!

149
00:05:08,447 --> 00:05:09,622
Now you know!
